  "generated_text": "1. The area of the region is given as 294 square centimeters.\n2. The region is formed by six congruent squares.\n3. To find the area of one square, we divide the total area by the number of squares:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one square} = \\frac{294}{6} = 49 \\text{ square centimeters}\n   \\]\n4. The area of a square is given by the square of its side length. Therefore, the side length of one square is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Side length of one square} = \\sqrt{49} = 7 \\text{ centimeters}\n   \\]\n5. The perimeter of the region is the sum of the lengths of all the sides of the six squares. Since each square has a side length of 7 centimeters, and there are 6 squares, the total perimeter is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Perimeter} = 6 \\times 4 \\times 7 = 6 \\times 28 = 84 \\text{ centimeters}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the region is 84 centimeters.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[84, '84']",
    "gold_answer": "If the area formed by 6 congruent squares is 294, the area formed by one of these squares is $294/6 = 49$. Thus, the side of each square is 7.\n\nThere are 8 horizontal sides and 6 vertical sides in the perimeter, for a total of 14 sides. Thus, the perimeter of this region is $14\\cdot 7 = \\boxed{98}$.",
    "is_correct": false
  },
